# The rule this instance ran under before Owner Terminals existed, kept here only
# as an explicit, reviewed opt-out. setup.sh installs the narrowed 90-wilhelmpa
# (in this same directory) by default; pass --sudo-policy=legacy-nopasswd to
# install this file instead, e.g. while the orchestrator is still auditing what
# to put in VOLITION_DEPLOY/VOLITION_STATUS and does not want the browser
# terminal's "password required" setting enforced yet.
#
# Installing this file makes every `sudo` command passwordless everywhere
# wilhelmpa runs one, including inside an owner-terminal browser session --
# sudo cannot distinguish that from the SSH automation this rule exists for (see
# 90-wilhelmpa's own comment). Switch back with --sudo-policy=narrow once ready.
wilhelmpa ALL=(ALL:ALL) NOPASSWD: ALL
